# NEGATIVE: the unlowered builtin cast-name CALLS must be rejected at
# check time. `int8`…`uint64`, `uint`, `float32`/`float64`, `byte` are in
# the resolver's `is_builtin` list but have NO lowering — the emitted C
# got raw extern calls (`undefined reference to 'int8'`). The supported
# conversion is the `as` cast (`x as int8`). `int`/`float`/`bool` HAVE
# real cast lowerings and stay callable.
void main():
    int8 x = int8(3)
    print(x)
